Aerie-Purpose: Register the Aerie Guard page action (the address bar icon of the Filter Engine) with the page action framework.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui/actions/chrome_action_id.h, chrome/browser/ui/page_action (action_ids.h, page_action_icon_type.h, page_action_properties_provider.cc), components/browser_apis/ui_controllers/toolbar/toolbar_ui_api_data_model.mojom, chrome/browser/ui/webui/webui_toolbar/utils/toolbar_button_utils.cc, tools/metrics/histograms/metadata/page
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #99. kActionAerieGuard sits in kActionIds after the JS optimizations action, so
the bookmark star stays last (the static_assert is untouched). Its properties are not
ephemeral (the icon shows on every http and https page) and its type is
PageActionIconType::kAerieGuard = 50, with the pair in enums.xml and the AerieGuard
variant of the PageActionType histograms. Helium's kHiddenPageActionIds is not touched,
so Helium's hide-page-actions flag hides the whole container, Guard included.
The mojom enum and the two switches in toolbar_button_utils.cc must list every action id
(the switches have no default), so they get the new id too.

